# Force LF line endings for all text files, regardless of each contributor's
# global core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# autocrlf=true silently converts LF to CRLF, which breaks anything that
# reads checked-out files byte-for-byte -- notably tools/install.sh's
# SHA256SUMS verification (confirmed broken by exactly this gap; see WO
# 2026-08-21-002). `eol=lf` fixes the checkout regardless of local config;
# `text=auto` lets Git still detect genuinely binary files automatically.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch/PowerShell files are conventionally CRLF, but LF works fine
# for both cmd.exe and PowerShell -- keeping everything LF avoids any
# checkout depending on which OS/tool last touched a file.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
